---
description: Java backend rules
globs:
  - "server/**/*.java"
  - "server/**/*.xml"
  - "server/**/*.yml"
  - "server/**/*.yaml"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use Java 21 and the approved Spring Boot baseline.
- Prefer constructor injection.
- Controllers only validate transport input and map output.
- Application services orchestrate use cases and transactions.
- Domain objects contain business rules and must not depend on Spring Web, JPA implementations or AI SDK classes.
- Infrastructure implements ports declared by the application/domain layers.
- External provider requests require connect/read timeouts and bounded retry.
- Use typed configuration properties instead of scattered environment lookups.
- Public write endpoints must support authorization, ownership validation and idempotency where applicable.
- Use RFC 7807-compatible problem responses or the project-standard error envelope.
- Add unit tests for domain logic and integration tests for persistence/API boundaries.
